  "label": "ANSWER",
  "response": "Yes, it is the right time to apply the remaining half of the urea. The manual recommends applying half of the urea at planting and the remaining half 30-45 days after planting. Since you planted 38 days ago, you are within this recommended window.",
  "justification": "The document states in Section 3.8 (Page 12) and Section 2 (Page 5) that for garlic production, 'half rate of urea is applied during planting and remaining is applied 30-45 days after planting.' The farmer's situation (38 days post-planting) falls squarely within this 30-45 day range.",
  "cited_pages": [5, 12]
}
